---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import GuideList from "../components/GuideList.astro";
import { tools, rows, comparisons } from "../data/catalog";

const home = comparisons["ga-alternatives"];
const table = rows(home.ids, home.highlight);
const description =
  "A DataFast review, pricing, and comparisons for founders. DataFast is the revenue tool to trial when the question is which channel brings paying customers, and Plausible, Fathom, GA4, or PostHog when a different job fits.";
---
<Base title="DataFast review, pricing, and comparisons for founders" description={description}>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">DataFast, compared with the alternatives</p>
          <h1>DataFast review, pricing, and <span class="grad">comparisons for founders</span></h1>
          <p class="lede">Independent notes on DataFast, the revenue analytics tool at datafa.st, for founders, indie hackers, and SaaS owners. The ranking follows one question: which channel brings paying customers. A different tool is the fit when the question is different.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <Button href="/reviews/datafast/">Read the DataFast review</Button>
            <Button href="/pricing/datafast/" variant="secondary">DataFast pricing</Button>
          </div>
          <p class="compared">Compared in this guide: <strong>DataFast, Plausible, Fathom, PostHog, GA4, Mixpanel</strong></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="hero-card" aria-label="Illustrative revenue breakdown">
          <div class="hero-card-head">
            <h2>Our pick for revenue</h2>
            <span class="sticker">Example</span>
          </div>
          <p class="pick-label">DataFast</p>
          <p class="pick-role">Best when you want to see which marketing channel brings paying customers.</p>
          <div class="bars">
            <div class="bar-row"><span class="name">Organic</span><div class="track"><div class="fill w48"></div></div><span class="amt">48%</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span class="name">X / social</span><div class="track"><div class="fill w24"></div></div><span class="amt">24%</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span class="name">Direct</span><div class="track"><div class="fill w18"></div></div><span class="amt">18%</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span class="name">Referral</span><div class="track"><div class="fill w10"></div></div><span class="amt">10%</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-card-foot">Starter from $9/mo · Illustrative channel mix, not a MetricsPick measurement.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-picks" id="picks" aria-labelledby="picks-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="picks-title">Top picks, by job to be done</h2>
          <p>One tool rarely wins every job. DataFast is the pick when the question is which channel brings paying customers. It is not a full replacement for PostHog, Mixpanel, or Amplitude. <a href="/alternatives/amplitude/">Amplitude has its own guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="picks">
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="datafast">
            <span class="pick-badge">Our pick for revenue</span>
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>DataFast</h3><span class="role">Revenue-first web analytics</span></div>
            <p>Best when you want a simple view of which marketing channel brings paying customers, joined to Stripe and the other payment tools DataFast documents.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.datafast.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links">
              <AffiliateLink placement="home-pick">Visit DataFast</AffiliateLink>
              <Button href="/reviews/datafast/" variant="secondary" size="sm">Read the review</Button>
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="plausible">
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>Plausible</h3><span class="role">Best lightweight privacy analytics</span></div>
            <p>A clean, cookieless traffic picture. Revenue tracking sits on the Business plan, not on every tier.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.plausible.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links"><Button href="/alternatives/plausible/" variant="secondary" size="sm">Read the overview</Button></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="fathom">
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>Fathom</h3><span class="role">Best simple privacy-first analytics</span></div>
            <p>Minimal, fast, and easy to explain to a client. Fathom’s pricing page includes event and revenue tracking on every plan.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.fathom.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links"><Button href="/alternatives/fathom-analytics/" variant="secondary" size="sm">Read the overview</Button></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="posthog">
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>PostHog</h3><span class="role">Best product analytics suite</span></div>
            <p>Session replay, feature flags, funnels and events in one product suite. Right when you are instrumenting a product, not only a marketing site.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.posthog.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links"><Button href="/pricing/posthog/" variant="secondary" size="sm">See pricing notes</Button></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="ga4">
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>Google Analytics 4</h3><span class="role">Best if you already live in Google</span></div>
            <p>Free, everywhere, and deep if you invest the time. The cost is complexity, cookies, and a setup many small teams leave half finished.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.ga4.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links"><Button href="/alternatives/google-analytics/" variant="secondary" size="sm">GA4 alternatives</Button></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pick-card" data-tool="mixpanel">
            <div class="pick-top"><h3>Mixpanel</h3><span class="role">Best event analytics for product teams</span></div>
            <p>Strong event and cohort analysis for product usage. A heavy fit if you only need to know which campaign brought the last ten payments.</p>
            <p class="price">{tools.mixpanel.priceLabel}</p>
            <p class="card-links"><Button href="/alternatives/mixpanel/" variant="secondary" size="sm">See alternatives</Button></p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-compare" id="compare" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="compare-title">Quick compare</h2>
          <p>A snapshot of focus, revenue attribution, and cookies. Starting prices as of 24 November 2026.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="compare">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Tool</th>
                <th>Best for</th>
                <th>Revenue attribution</th>
                <th>Cookies</th>
                <th>Starting price</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {table.map((row) => (
                <tr class={row.highlight ? "is-pick" : undefined}>
                  <td data-label="Tool"><strong>{row.name}</strong></td>
                  <td data-label="Best for">{row.bestFor}</td>
                  <td data-label="Attribution" class={row.attributionTone}>{row.attribution}</td>
                  <td data-label="Cookies">{row.cookies}</td>
                  <td data-label="Price" class="price">{row.price}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="table-note">{home.note} Amplitude’s free tier is covered on the <a href="/pricing/amplitude/">Amplitude pricing</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-hubs" id="hubs" aria-labelledby="hubs-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="hubs-title">Explore by topic</h2>
          <p>Every guide lives under a content-type path, with a hub page and breadcrumbs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hubs">
          <a class="hub" href="/alternatives/"><h3>Alternatives</h3><p>Tools like GA4, PostHog or Mixpanel, ranked by the job they actually do.</p><span class="go">/alternatives/</span></a>
          <a class="hub" href="/pricing/"><h3>Pricing</h3><p>What a plan actually costs as events, seats or sites grow.</p><span class="go">/pricing/</span></a>
          <a class="hub" href="/compare/"><h3>Compare</h3><p>Side-by-side matchups, starting with PostHog and Google Analytics.</p><span class="go">/compare/</span></a>
          <a class="hub" href="/reviews/"><h3>Reviews</h3><p>Hands-on reading of public docs, including where a tool falls short.</p><span class="go">/reviews/</span></a>
          <a class="hub" href="/guides/"><h3>Guides</h3><p>Attribution, cookieless tracking, and how to choose a stack.</p><span class="go">/guides/</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-cluster" id="datafast" aria-labelledby="datafast-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="datafast-title">The DataFast cluster</h2>
          <p>Start here if the question is DataFast itself: what it is, what datafa.st charges, how the API and MCP work, and how it compares with Plausible and GA4. The broader guides sit below this list.</p>
        </div>
        <GuideList
          items={[
            {
              href: "/reviews/datafast/",
              title: "DataFast analytics review",
              description: "What the tool at datafa.st is, who makes it, and when not to buy it.",
            },
            {
              href: "/pricing/datafast/",
              title: "DataFast pricing",
              description: "The datafa.st homepage ladder: Starter from $9 a month and Growth from $19.",
            },
            {
              href: "/guides/datafast-api/",
              title: "DataFast API and docs",
              description: "How to send goal events and revenue, plus the CLI and MCP.",
            },
            {
              href: "/guides/datafast-mcp/",
              title: "DataFast MCP",
              description: "The remote server at datafa.st/api/mcp, and what an assistant still cannot do.",
            },
            {
              href: "/alternatives/datafast/",
              title: "DataFast alternatives",
              description: "Plausible, Fathom, GA4, PostHog, and when staying with DataFast is the better call.",
            },
            {
              href: "/compare/datafast-vs-plausible/",
              title: "DataFast vs Plausible",
              description: "Revenue attribution beside a cookieless traffic dashboard. Both have a published starting price of $9.",
            },
            {
              href: "/compare/datafast-vs-google-analytics/",
              title: "DataFast vs Google Analytics",
              description: "A paid revenue report next to free GA4, and when founders keep both.",
            },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-guides" id="guides" aria-labelledby="guides-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="guides-title">More guides</h2>
          <p>Broader starting points, after the DataFast pages above. Each one compares several tools and links out to the vendors.</p>
        </div>
        <GuideList
          items={[
            {
              href: "/alternatives/google-analytics/",
              title: "The best Google Analytics alternatives for founders",
              description: "When GA4 is more dashboard than answer, and which lighter tools actually show revenue.",
            },
            {
              href: "/guides/marketing-attribution-tools/",
              title: "Marketing attribution tools, compared",
              description: "How to tell a click from a customer without standing up a full enterprise stack.",
            },
            {
              href: "/guides/cookieless-analytics/",
              title: "Cookieless analytics: what you gain and lose",
              description: "Privacy-friendly scripts, rotating identifiers, and the trade-off for long revenue journeys.",
            },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section s-trust" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="method-title">How we test, and how we get paid</h2>
          <p>Independence is the product. Affiliate relationships are labeled, never hidden.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust">
          <article class="trust-card">
            <h3>How we test</h3>
            <p>Prices and product behavior come from public docs and pricing pages, dated when they were current. Limits sit next to strengths. There are no invented benchmark scores. <a href="/how-we-test/">Read the method</a>.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="trust-card">
            <h3>Independence</h3>
            <p>metricspick is not a DataFast site. Recommendations follow the job to be done. If a heavier tool like PostHog is the honest fit, we say so. <a href="/about/">About the site</a>.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="trust-card">
            <h3>Affiliate disclosure</h3>
            <p>Some DataFast links are affiliate links. We may earn a commission if you subscribe, at no extra cost to you. Other tools are reviewed whether or not a program exists. <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Full disclosure</a>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
